{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A failed install or process replacement can leave the old release with incompatible dependencies, breaking a later restart."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A transient update failure leaves the worker unavailable for jobs until it is manually restarted, even after the coordinator changes releases."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A stale update warning persists and masks current setup warnings, but it does not affect worker availability."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"compat","trigger":"plausible","reason":"After an update failure, rolling back the coordinator causes its strict heartbeat schema to reject the new warning field and stop the worker."}]}